From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:34:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Skip interconnect updates when no input is
 pending

Scale power stops its clock update when the source queue has no
payload, but still recalculates the interconnect vote. On Piano this
alternates the memory path between the minimum and the active vote at
the frame rate while playing H.264. Capture buffers can be queued
in between input submissions.

Match the Qualcomm VIDC driver's no-pending-input behavior and skip
the interconnect update along with the clock update. Subsequent input
continues to update its vote, and runtime suspend still clears both
paths.

Codex analyzed Piano's interconnect trace, compared the empty queue
path against the Qualcomm driver, tested six paths on the host, and
compiled the changed object with ARM64 Kbuild.

Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8750/blob/d50b305f7da9e14715a25120a4ac7b1a4b8b97c3/vendor/qcom/opensource/video-driver/driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_power.c#L509-L610
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c
index 91aa21d40..8969982df 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ int iris_scale_power(struct iris_inst *inst)
 	}
 
 	ret = iris_scale_clocks(inst);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret || !inst->max_input_data_size)
 		return ret;
 
 	return iris_vote_interconnects(inst);
